#
# Finding #44 (myrocks-notes/port-findings.md): with
# rocksdb_write_policy=write_unprepared, a transaction that was rolled back
# before a server kill comes back after the restart.
#
# The scenarios are those of rocksdb.innodb_port_lob_rollback_crash, run under
# write_unprepared with rocksdb_write_batch_flush_threshold=1 (see the
# -master.opt file):
#   1. kill with a large transaction still open, restart;
#   2. kill while ROLLBACK is running, restart;
#   3. kill right after ROLLBACK returned, restart.
# After round 3 the recovered data must equal the committed data. On the
# current build, recovery reports "Found 1 prepared transaction(s) in ROCKSDB"
# and "Successfully committed 1 internal transaction(s)", and the inserts and
# updates of the rolled-back transaction are visible. Round 3 alone, or rounds
# 2 and 3, recover correctly; round 1 followed by round 3 fails every time.
#
# The expected result is the one write_committed and write_prepared produce.
# This test is disabled in collections/disabled.def until #44 is fixed.
#
--source include/have_rocksdb.inc
--source include/not_valgrind.inc
--source include/not_crashrep.inc

SELECT @@global.rocksdb_write_policy, @@global.rocksdb_write_batch_flush_threshold;
--source suite/rocksdb/t/innodb_port_lob_rollback_crash.test
